OPERATOR DECISION / APPEND

SRC-125 has been reviewed against its exact canonical body.

It does NOT contain a real credential requiring quarantine or source replacement.

The current SOURCE_CREDENTIALS_UNSAFE result is a false positive in the generic credential-assignment detector.

ROOT CAUSE

The benign source contains:

    ... coupled to a literal STYLE token:
    - centralize only that CURRENT_STYLE_FIXTURE authority;

The current generic assignment patterns in intake.py use `\s*` around the assignment separator/value boundary.

Because `\s` includes newlines, the detector interprets:

    token:
    -

as if `-` were a credential value.

This affects both:
- `_looks_sensitive(...)`
- `_CREDENTIAL_ASSIGNMENT_RE` / `_redact_text(...)`

The canonical codec high-confidence credential patterns are not the defect.

DO NOT:
- quarantine SRC-125 merely to bypass this false positive;
- rewrite or sanitize SRC-125;
- mutate its exact authoritative body;
- mark a false credential finding as accepted baseline;
- weaken high-confidence credential detection.

Create one bounded P1 repair owner if canonical protocol requires a ticket.

REQUIRED FIX

Constrain generic key/value assignment whitespace to the same physical line.

Prefer horizontal whitespace only around `:` / `=`, e.g. spaces/tabs rather than a newline-crossing `\s*`.

The intended semantic rule is:

A generic credential assignment may match:

    token: abc
    token = abc
    password: abc
    secret = abc

but must NOT match:

    STYLE token:
    - documentation bullet

or equivalent CRLF/LF multiline prose.

Keep the actual credential value non-whitespace and same-line.

REQUIRED RED/GREEN CONTROLS

1. Reproduce the current defect with the exact semantic shape:

       "literal STYLE token:\n- centralize ..."

   Pre-fix:
   - `_looks_sensitive` reports sensitive and/or `_redact_text` changes the text.

   Post-fix:
   - `_looks_sensitive` is false for this benign case;
   - `_redact_text` returns byte-equivalent text.

2. Repeat with CRLF:

       "literal STYLE token:\r\n- centralize ..."

   It must also remain unchanged.

3. Same-line real assignments must remain detected/redacted:

       token: realvalue
       token = realvalue
       password: realvalue
       secret = realvalue

4. Existing high-confidence patterns must remain unchanged:
   GitHub-style tokens, AWS keys, OpenAI-style keys, bearer credentials and credential-bearing database URIs must retain their current protection.

5. `<redacted>` and existing masked forms must retain their current semantics.

6. No multiline prose may become credential authority merely because a following line starts with punctuation or a bullet.

LIVE ACCEPTANCE

After the focused repair:

- re-run the existing source credential/quarantine suites;
- re-run source receipt and source release-gate neighbors affected by this detector;
- evaluate SRC-125 again using its EXACT EXISTING BYTES;
- SRC-125 must no longer produce SOURCE_CREDENTIALS_UNSAFE;
- its canonical body digest must remain unchanged;
- do not replace SRC-125 with a sanitized derivative;
- do not manually edit its metadata merely to clear the gate.

